  Here is an algorithm to find the first non-repeating character in a given string:

1. Initialize an empty character array `char_array` to store the characters of the input string.
2. Initialize a variable `i` to 0, which will be used to iterate through the characters of the input string.
3. While `i` is less than the length of the input string, do the following:
	* Check if the character at index `i` is the same as the character at index `i-1`. If it is, then move on to the next character without storing it in the `char_array`.
	* Otherwise, store the character at index `i` in the `char_array`.
4. Once you have iterated through the entire input string, the `char_array` will contain all the unique characters in the string, and you can return the first non-repeating character in the array.

Here is some sample pseudocode to illustrate the algorithm:
```
function find_first_non_repeating_char(str) {
  // Initialize an empty character array to store the characters of the input string
  char_array = []

  // Initialize a variable to iterate through the characters of the input string
  i = 0

  // While i is less than the length of the input string, do the following:
  while i < str.length {
    // Check if the character at index i is the same as the character at index i-1
    if str[i] == str[i-1] {
      // If it is, move on to the next character without storing it in the char_array
      i += 1
      continue
    }

    // Otherwise, store the character at index i in the char_array
    char_array.push(str[i])
    i += 1
  }

  // Return the first non-repeating character in the char_array
  return char_array[0]
}
```
This algorithm has a time complexity of O(n), where n is the length of the input string, and a space complexity of O(1), as the array `char_array` is only used to store the unique characters in the input string and has a fixed size.

