  There are several algorithms you can use to find the closest pair of points from a given set of points in JavaScript. Here are a few options:

1. Brute Force Algorithm:

This algorithm involves iterating through the set of points and comparing the distance between each pair of points. The point pair with the smallest distance is the closest pair. Here is an example of how you could implement this algorithm in JavaScript:
```
function closestPointPair(points) {
  let closestPair = null;
  let minDistance = Infinity;

  for (let i = 0; i < points.length; i++) {
    for (let j = i + 1; j < points.length; j++) {
      const distance = Math.sqrt(Math.pow(points[i].x - points[j].x, 2) + Math.pow(points[i].y - points[j].y, 2));
      if (closestPair === null || distance < minDistance) {
        closestPair = [points[i], points[j]];
        minDistance = distance;
      }
    }
  }

  return closestPair;
}
```
2. Dynamic Programming Algorithm:

This algorithm is more efficient than the brute force algorithm because it uses dynamic programming to find the closest pair of points. It works by building a two-dimensional matrix of distances between each pair of points, and then finding the minimum distance in the matrix. Here is an example of how you could implement this algorithm in JavaScript:
```
function closestPointPair(points) {
  const n = points.length;
  const dp = new Array(n);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    dp[i] = new Array(n);
    for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) {
      dp[i][j] = Infinity;
    }
  }

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
      const distance = Math.sqrt(Math.pow(points[i].x - points[j].x, 2) + Math.pow(points[i].y - points[j].y, 2));
      dp[i][j] = Math.min(dp[i][j], distance);
    }
  }

  return [dp[0][n - 1], dp[n - 1][0]];
}
```
3. Nearest Neighbor Algorithm:

This algorithm is similar to the brute force algorithm, but it uses a different approach to find the closest pair of points. Instead of comparing the distance between each pair of points, it uses a nearest neighbor search algorithm to find the closest point to a given point. Here is an example of how you could implement this algorithm in JavaScript:
```
function closestPointPair(points) {
  const nearestNeighbor = new NearestNeighbor(points);
  return nearestNeighbor.findClosest();
}

class NearestNeighbor {
  constructor(points) {
    this.points = points;
    this.distances = new Array(points.length);
  }

  findClosest() {
    const closest = null;
    const distance = Infinity;

    for (let i = 0; i < this.points.length; i++) {
      const distanceToPoint = Math.sqrt(Math.pow(this.points[i].x - this.points[closest].x, 2) + Math.pow(this.points[i].y - this.points[closest].y, 2));
      if (distance > distanceToPoint) {
        closest = i;
        distance = distanceToPoint;
      }
    }

    return [closest, distance];
  }
}
```
These are just a few examples of algorithms you can use to find the closest pair of points from a given set of points in JavaScript. There are many other algorithms you could use, depending on the specific requirements of your application.

